1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,925
THERE IS NO RELATION
TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

3
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,067
Are you okay?

4
00:01:37,598 --> 00:01:38,599
Yeah.

5
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:42,060
I'm fine.

6
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:02,581
Oh, uh…

7
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:06,251
Whoa!

8
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:18,221
NEW JAPANESE FOR TOTAL BEGINNERS

9
00:02:18,305 --> 00:02:21,350
EPISODE 3

10
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:31,318
Was it all right
that I let him in?

11
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:40,494
-Uh…
-Oh, uh…

12
00:02:41,203 --> 00:02:44,289
- Right here. Sofa. Uh-huh. Tonight.
- Oh. Sofa. Sofa.

13
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:46,625
I can sleep here?

14
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:48,543
- Okay, okay.
- Yes, good night.

15
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:49,628
Thank you.

16
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:52,798
About that.

17
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:56,426
Uh…

18
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:02,015
That figurine.

19
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:05,143
Mmm. That one…

20
00:03:05,227 --> 00:03:07,646
- Oh, this?
- Yeah, um… Ah!

21
00:03:08,814 --> 00:03:10,440
- This?
- Yeah.

22
00:03:11,108 --> 00:03:13,985
Do you like that character?

23
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,407
Uh, no, that's not why.

24
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:20,909
I'm holding it for someone else.

25
00:03:26,415 --> 00:03:28,083
- Holding on to it?
- Mm-hmm.

26
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:31,503
Oh, the Korean guy
I told you about earlier

27
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:33,630
bought this as a souvenir for his son.

28
00:03:42,556 --> 00:03:44,766
Is there anything else
you know about that man?

29
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:50,147
Um, I was very little…

30
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:54,693
Ah…

31
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,863
I do have some
of Mr. Gyeongsu's belongings.

32
00:04:03,702 --> 00:04:06,413
My grandpa put everything
in this suitcase.

33
00:04:07,539 --> 00:04:11,168
We've been holding on to all of it
hoping someone will come to collect them.

34
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:20,886
Maybe that's why you're here?

35
00:04:23,138 --> 00:04:27,851
No, just curious
because you said he was Korean. Hmm.

36
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:35,358
They always worked together.

37
00:04:36,193 --> 00:04:39,738
Researching different ways
to successfully grow crops here.

38
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:57,172
How many photos are you going to take?

39
00:04:57,255 --> 00:04:58,548
They're so cute, aren't they?

40
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:02,302
Every day you're snapping away.

41
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:03,887
How are you not tired of that yet?

42
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:07,182
Watching them grow brings me joy.

43
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:10,143
Like how watching
Karin grow makes you happy.

44
00:05:10,644 --> 00:05:11,645
It's sort of similar.

45
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:13,063
Oh.

46
00:05:13,814 --> 00:05:14,940
Karin.

47
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:20,403
Someday my son might come visit.

48
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:24,658
Will you take care of this one
so that he can see it?

49
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:27,327
Yes, sir. Thanks for trusting me.

50
00:05:31,915 --> 00:05:33,333
<i>He was so kind.</i>

51
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:35,043
And he smiled a lot.

52
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:51,434
Well, I need to go to bed.

53
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:52,519
Oh, right.

54
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:56,147
I'll clean up in here before I go.

55
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:00,694
- Sleep well, all right?
- Yeah.

56
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:26,094
GENERAL PRINCIPLES OF SOIL
AND FERTILIZERS

57
00:06:42,777 --> 00:06:44,321
<i>New shoots sprouted today.</i>

58
00:06:45,155 --> 00:06:47,532
<i>How cold and hard it must've been</i>
<i>beneath the soil.</i>

59
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:50,869
<i>It's amazing how they were</i>
<i>able to break through it.</i>

60
00:06:52,287 --> 00:06:55,915
<i>It somewhat reminded me</i>
<i>of the day Yubin started school.</i>

61
00:06:57,626 --> 00:07:00,879
<i>I kept looking back at him in front</i>
<i>of the school gates, watching him go in…</i>

62
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:03,131
<i>Worried he might snap,</i>

63
00:07:03,214 --> 00:07:05,342
<i>like the sprouts that had</i>
<i>just barely made it out of the soil…</i>

64
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:09,095
<i>While these strawberries continue</i>
<i>to rise toward me above the ground…</i>

65
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:12,891
<i>Before I knew it, my son was growing up,</i>
<i>leaving my arms.</i>

66
00:07:13,892 --> 00:07:15,727
<i>They're both thriving, and yet…</i>

67
00:07:16,478 --> 00:07:18,104
<i>It's a strange feeling.</i>

68
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:22,734
<i>I think I miss him very much tonight.</i>

69
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,550
I better wake him up I guess.

70
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,756
Wow.

71
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,885
He's got long lashes.

72
00:08:50,447 --> 00:08:54,159
Oh, uh… The alarm…
I forgot to turn it off, uh…

73
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:02,125
Huh?

74
00:09:10,425 --> 00:09:12,302
Why is my heart pounding so hard?

75
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:18,516
Uh… "Let's meet at the farm later."

76
00:09:21,061 --> 00:09:22,771
You don't have to come to work today.

77
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:24,898
Why not?

78
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:29,527
Uh, um, actually…
We're having a village meeting today.

79
00:09:39,496 --> 00:09:42,373
He must have been close
with all the villagers.

80
00:09:46,503 --> 00:09:47,670
"I'm coming with you."

81
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:53,009
-Why is that?
-Uh, I'm coming with you.

82
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,387
-Why is that?
-I'm coming with--

83
00:09:56,971 --> 00:10:00,391
Uh-huh. Uh… Um, why is that?

84
00:10:02,894 --> 00:10:04,854
- Mr. Ikeda.
- Oh, Mr. Ikeda.

85
00:10:04,938 --> 00:10:06,815
-I'm so glad you're here.
-Hello there! Nice to see you.

86
00:10:06,898 --> 00:10:07,899
-Come on.
-Let's go in.

87
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,067
NEIGHBORHOOD COMMUNITY CENTER

88
00:10:17,784 --> 00:10:20,703
- Well, look who the cat dragged in.
- Hmm?

89
00:10:21,538 --> 00:10:22,705
This guy.

90
00:10:22,789 --> 00:10:25,542
He's a new employee
who started working for Karin.

91
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:39,264
-Uh…
-Come in. Say hi to everyone.

92
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:46,187
Uh… Uh…

93
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:47,397
Hi.

94
00:10:47,981 --> 00:10:49,732
Go-Good morning.

95
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:52,068
- I'm Yubin.
- Good morning.

96
00:10:52,152 --> 00:10:54,487
Good morning.

97
00:10:54,571 --> 00:10:55,572
Morning.

98
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:09,544
Ah, so he's Karin's new helper.

99
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:13,298
He's got quite a body,
and he's nice to look at.

100
00:11:13,381 --> 00:11:14,841
-Hey.
-That's inappropriate.

101
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:17,385
I bet you that he won't last here
very long.

102
00:11:18,011 --> 00:11:22,974
He needs to have dedication too. It takes
much more than a sturdy body, doesn't it?

103
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,100
Mm-hmm.

104
00:11:24,184 --> 00:11:25,393
Hello there. Hi.

105
00:11:28,229 --> 00:11:31,024
- Good morning, everyone!
- Good morning.

106
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:33,526
Let's all get this meeting started,
shall we?

107
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:38,781
Good news.

108
00:11:38,865 --> 00:11:42,702
Green Nova Corporation Festa
will be held again this year!

109
00:11:45,914 --> 00:11:49,459
We have another wonderful opportunity
to be part of the Festa,

110
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:51,294
thanks to every one of you here.

111
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:54,297
Everyone, uh, has a handout, right?

112
00:11:55,173 --> 00:11:58,009
The agenda for this meeting
is on the first page.

113
00:11:58,092 --> 00:12:00,428
- What's Green Nova Festa?
- Ah.

114
00:12:01,596 --> 00:12:04,599
It's a pretty big event
where we get to promote our produce.

115
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:08,394
<i>It's held by the biggest</i>
<i>agricultural company in all of Japan.</i>

116
00:12:08,895 --> 00:12:12,523
<i>Every region brings their</i>
<i>signature produce to compete and sell.</i>

117
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:16,527
<i>This year, it's going to be Karin</i>
<i>whose crops will be evaluated.</i>

118
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:19,864
- Ah.
- All right.

119
00:12:19,948 --> 00:12:21,741
Together there are four candidates.

120
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:24,786
The first candidate
is "Karin's Strawberries."

121
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:28,164
- My farm's strengths are that…
- Isn't she amazing?

122
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:30,792
…the strawberries
can be grown in large quantities,

123
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:32,293
and they're great quality.

124
00:12:32,377 --> 00:12:34,420
So I really hope you all are pleased.

125
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:35,588
Wow.

126
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:38,883
How does Mari make
turning pages look so chic?

127
00:12:38,967 --> 00:12:42,845
…and created a whole
presentation, including drawings.

128
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:47,767
Next up are the sweet potatoes
we proudly showcase every year.

129
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,186
We've been consistent on the amount
we produce,

130
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:53,815
so I'm pretty sure we'll be able
to showcase them again.

131
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:56,192
Advertising them will be very important.

132
00:12:56,276 --> 00:12:57,860
- Uh…
- Yes, please go ahead.

133
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,530
It's good to remember…

134
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:02,657
That way we can make it
a little more special…

135
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:09,330
All right, why don't we continue
this conversation outside while we eat.

136
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:12,750
Time for lunch.

137
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:14,961
We're going to eat first.

138
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:17,380
Eat first? Oh, okay.

139
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:21,509
- It's yummy, right?
- So hungry.

140
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:23,386
-Tell me when. Okay.
-That's enough.

141
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:24,595
This looks refreshing.

142
00:13:24,679 --> 00:13:26,306
This works out great.

143
00:13:29,017 --> 00:13:31,102
He's so handsome. Look at him.

144
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:41,821
Kunam, Mari.
Thanks for being our Festa cheering squad.

145
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,406
Of course. Happy to help.

146
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:47,827
I'm perfect. These guns, nice smile,
and cute.

147
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:49,787
I'll charm them all.

148
00:13:49,871 --> 00:13:51,164
You can count on me.

149
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:53,750
Yeah!

150
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:55,793
- You've got this!
- Go, Kunam!

151
00:13:55,877 --> 00:13:58,463
Why me? Why am I paired with Kunam?

152
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:01,591
'Cause I mean, what about…

153
00:14:04,469 --> 00:14:08,473
Our Kunam is so cute and charming, but…

154
00:14:09,307 --> 00:14:12,185
Yeah, but this year's Festa is very…

155
00:14:12,727 --> 00:14:14,687
Very important for us.

156
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:19,942
Hey, come here a minute.

157
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:27,283
Why is everyone staring at me?

158
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:29,452
Hey, Kunam!
What did he say?

159
00:14:32,663 --> 00:14:33,664
You see that?

160
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:35,792
Right, my company went bust. So what?

161
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:38,795
What? Why is he angry?

162
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:40,838
He… He can't do it.

163
00:14:40,922 --> 00:14:42,006
Oh.

164
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:48,221
Yubin is really famous in Korea,
but he made mistakes.

165
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:53,810
So he has to lay low here for a while.
Uh, he has to avoid the loan sharks.

166
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:01,484
-Oh, I knew he was trouble.
-A troublemaker?

167
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,027
See?

168
00:15:03,111 --> 00:15:08,449
What'd you tell them?
Why are they all staring at me like that?

169
00:15:08,533 --> 00:15:10,118
Oh…

170
00:15:10,201 --> 00:15:12,537
They want your help
with the designs for the Festa.

171
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,622
You've done that a lot, right?
Come on, man.

172
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:17,667
How am I supposed to do designs
for a rural event?

173
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,210
I've never done anything like that before.

174
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:23,005
This means everything to Karin.

175
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,758
You said you had to make good with her.

176
00:15:26,551 --> 00:15:28,010
This is for Karin.

177
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:41,566
Fine, fine. I'll do it.

178
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:46,737
Instead,
he'll be in charge of our designs!

179
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:48,865
Give him a round of applause!

180
00:15:54,162 --> 00:15:57,039
-Oh, what a sweet man.
-Oh! So nice.

181
00:15:59,834 --> 00:16:01,460
Thank you very much.
Thank you.

182
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:03,713
Eat up and do your best.

183
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:05,840
-Come on. Now eat.
-You must be hungry.

184
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:08,050
- Is it good?
- Come by our shop any time.

185
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:10,761
Thank you.

186
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:14,849
- Is it good?
- Hmm?

187
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:17,393
Hmm?

188
00:16:19,395 --> 00:16:21,022
Thank you so much.

189
00:16:22,356 --> 00:16:23,649
Bye-bye.

190
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:36,704
Kunam mentioned that you were
really famous in Korea.

191
00:16:38,164 --> 00:16:39,749
What brought you here?

192
00:16:41,459 --> 00:16:44,045
Ah. I'm just buying some prop…

193
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:47,548
What I meant was…

194
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:52,720
I've got a lot going on in Korea.
I just wanted to take a little break,

195
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:53,804
but…

196
00:16:55,473 --> 00:16:57,516
I really like it here.

197
00:16:58,517 --> 00:16:59,644
It's so relaxing.

198
00:17:03,606 --> 00:17:04,607
I see.

199
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:08,778
Anyway, thank you for volunteering.

200
00:17:09,654 --> 00:17:13,616
This Festa will make or break us.

201
00:17:15,952 --> 00:17:18,412
You can't tell from looking at them…

202
00:17:20,873 --> 00:17:24,085
but everyone's worried about
me doing farm work alone.

203
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:30,967
That's why this Festa's important.
If my strawberries get recognition,

204
00:17:31,801 --> 00:17:33,970
they'll realize I'm capable on my own,

205
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,180
and they'll be able to relax.

206
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:41,310
This is a pretty huge deal, huh?

207
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:43,229
Mm-hmm. Totally.

208
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:46,941
- In that case…
- Hmm?

209
00:17:47,984 --> 00:17:50,861
Since I'm helping you,
could you do me a favor?

210
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:55,992
What is it?

211
00:17:56,075 --> 00:17:57,618
Oh, please just let me sleep in here!

212
00:17:57,702 --> 00:18:00,830
Absolutely not. We are not
sleeping together in the same space.

213
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:01,914
Come on!

214
00:18:01,998 --> 00:18:03,207
- Stop it!
- Why "stop it," huh?

215
00:18:03,291 --> 00:18:04,625
Why "stop it"? No "stop it," no "stop it."

216
00:18:04,709 --> 00:18:06,877
-No way!
-You said you'd do whatever I want!

217
00:18:06,961 --> 00:18:08,879
- Why, "Stop it"? Tell me why!
- I said no!

218
00:18:08,963 --> 00:18:11,841
Remember when I got drenched last time?

219
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:13,926
I can't stay there!

220
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:15,845
It gets so cold and hot.

221
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:21,100
No matter how much I sweep,
there's always more dust!

222
00:18:21,183 --> 00:18:23,811
I'm allergic to dust.

223
00:18:23,894 --> 00:18:26,939
I'm just not going to last
if I keep on staying in that dump.

224
00:18:27,023 --> 00:18:29,775
For me, for you, and for the strawberries.

225
00:18:29,859 --> 00:18:33,696
We need to keep brainstorming together
so we can win first place in this Festa.

226
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:35,615
All right! Okay, listen!

227
00:18:35,698 --> 00:18:36,699
It's fine.

228
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:40,161
-I'll allow it.
-Huh?

229
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:42,913
But if you break any of the rules,
you are out of here.

230
00:18:42,997 --> 00:18:44,081
-Ru-rules? Rules?
-Rules.

231
00:18:44,165 --> 00:18:45,499
Oh? O-Okay. Rules.

232
00:18:45,583 --> 00:18:49,503
Okay, I'll sleep right here.
Okay? Okay, great.

233
00:18:49,587 --> 00:18:51,964
- Rules? Okay. Rules are good.
- Rules.

234
00:18:52,048 --> 00:18:53,758
Rules I really really like.

235
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:58,346
There are so many.

236
00:18:58,429 --> 00:19:00,431
But I can't read any of this.

237
00:19:03,309 --> 00:19:04,810
Rule number one.

238
00:19:04,894 --> 00:19:08,230
You are not to come out
to the living room after 11:00 p.m.

239
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:19,283
In particular, sleeping on that sofa
from now on is off limits.

240
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,161
What is this, prison?

241
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:23,245
Secondly.

242
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:25,456
At all times
you are to be properly dressed.

243
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,083
Even though it's indoors?

244
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,459
The third rule is,

245
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,127
that my room is off-limits.

246
00:19:33,255 --> 00:19:35,132
I don't even want to go in your room.

247
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:39,470
You can read
the rest of the rules on your own time.

248
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:42,264
4. YUBIN IN CHARGE OF
TAKING OUT ALL THE TRASH.

249
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:43,891
5. YUBIN ALSO IN CHARGE OF
